WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:03.160
Stitch pattern using DesignaKnit

2
00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:07.490
with your machine is accomplished
by sending data from your computer

3
00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:13.820
to the carriage, instructing the carriage
to select and position needles.

4
00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:17.920
Before you fast forward, please hang
in there with me for just a moment.

5
00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:21.020
It's important that you understand this.

6
00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:25.740
In general, stitch patterning is accomplished
by the position of the needles

7
00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:30.300
and how they pass through the channels
under the carriage.

8
00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:33.860
The channels are controlled
by the cam lever.

9
00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:39.820
The red line in this image indicates
the path that the needle butts take.

10
00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:43.940
Notice how the levers change
the configuration of the channel,

11
00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:47.300
therefore, the path
the needle butts travel.

12
00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:49.220
As the needle butts are directed

13
00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:53.300
through the channel, the needles
are positioned to form stitches.

14
00:00:53.330 --> 00:01:00.260
Each needle will either knit, slip, tuck,
or knit with a different yarn.

15
00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:03.700
Please remove your carriage, turn it over,

16
00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:09.700
hold it securely, shift the cam lever,
and observe what happens.

17
00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:13.360
In the following exercises,
we will explore the different stitch

18
00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:18.660
patterns available on your machine
and the steps for accomplishing them.

19
00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:21.380
But remember, it's DesignaKnit, sending

20
00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:25.780
signals to the carriage that determines
which needles pass

21
00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:30.420
through the path under the carriage,
and it's the cam lever that determines

22
00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:34.400
the configuration of the path
and which stitch type is formed.

